 block section at one time but trains must be run at low speed in order to stop on sight behind the train in front. Such working is often authorised to allow freight trains to \"bunch\" together to await a path through a bottleneck instead of being strung out over several block sections, as would be necessary if absolute working were in force.", "reference": "1962 October, “Talking of Trains: The collisions at Connington”, in Modern Railways, page 232:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "shlukovat se"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "shluknout se"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "ophopen"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "δεματιάζω"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αρμαθιάζω"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "arracimarse"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "enracimarse"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "fruncirse"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To be gathered together in folds", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive) To protrude or swell", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "A very large ſparry Nodule externally of a brown Colour. It has ſomewhat of the reſemblance of a large Champignon before 'tis open'd, bunching out into a large round Knob at one end, the part proceeding from it being leſs, round, and not unlike a Stalk.", "reference": "1729, J[ohn] Woodward, “Classis V. Corpora Coralloidea, & hisce affinia.”, in An Attempt towards a Natural History of the Fossils of England; […], tome I, London: […] F[rancis] Fayram, […]; J[ohn] Senex, […]; and J. Osborn and T[homas] Longman, […], →OCLC, part I (Of the Fossils that are Real and Natural: […]), page 144:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": ["cluster", "group"], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bunch", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}